      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-287045",
      ":question/problem": "A carpenter builds and sells square wooden tabletops. The selling price $P$, in dollars, of a tabletop is a linear function of the side length $s$, in feet, as shown in the table below.\n\n| Side length, $s$ (feet) | Price, $P$ (dollars) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $3$ | $37.00$ |\n| $5$ | $51.00$ |\n| $7$ | $65.00$ |\n\nWhich of the following could define the relationship between $s$ and $P$?"
